  "body": "Complete direct 3-CNF reduction for the source\u2019s aggregate all-root undirected spanning-tree objective. The explicitly encoded nonnegative-integer decision version is strongly NP-complete, with costs only 0, 1 and n+1. Includes unchanged proof and separate adversarial AI review: 78,056 author checks and 600,122 independent Pr\u00fcfer-tree/edge-cut checks, with NP membership, both reduction directions and noncanonical trees covered. Actual approach count is 2/5. The adjacent fixed-root directed path-cost problem has a related independently developed literal-selection mechanism; no equivalence or two unrelated discoveries are claimed. Novelty and human peer review are unestablished. Parent coordinates claimed_solved queue status.",
